 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "totalTask, totalModel, totalHuman and k are positive integers. Every task must receive exactly k assignments whose humans are pairwise different and whose models are pairwise different. Build the schedule greedily: take tasks t1, t2, ... in order and give each task k assignments one after another; for each assignment choose, among humans not yet used on this task, the one with the fewest assignments so far (smaller index on ties), and independently, among models not yet used on this task, the one with the fewest assignments so far (smaller index on ties). Return the assignments as [task, model, human] string triples in the order they were made, or [] when k exceeds totalHuman or totalModel.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk18-b-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
